# Cold Start Optimization — Research & Results

> Measured 2026-09-09 on g6e.xlarge (L40S, ap-south-2).
> Branch: `perf/s3-avatar-cache`

---

## Problem

Cold start without pre-built avatar cache takes **7+ minutes** (DWPose + VAE encode + geometry
for 1874 frames). Even with the pre-built cache on S3, the download + Python startup totalled
**53 seconds** in the initial implementation. The goal is to bring cold start as close to warm
start (~14s) as possible.

---

## Storage Architecture

```
Instance: g6e.xlarge (L40S GPU, 32GB RAM, 25 Gbps network)
EBS root:  gp3 150GB, 125 MB/s throughput (default), 3000 IOPS
NVMe SSD:  /opt/dlami/nvme — 232.8GB local instance store, ~2+ GB/s sequential
```

| Storage    | Write speed     | Persists across            | Cost     |
|------------|-----------------|----------------------------|----------|
| EBS gp3    | 149 MB/s (dd)   | Everything (durable)       | Included |
| NVMe local | 312 MB/s (dd direct), burst higher | Container restart ✓, instance stop ✗ | $0 |
| tmpfs      | Memory speed    | Nothing                    | Uses RAM |

